{
  "about": "The art style's environment rules as numbers (docs/art-style.md, \"Places\"; D356): for each place, the numbers of its vantage views (places.ts) held to its reference (looks/<name>.json), each under the rule it measures. `within` holds the mean of the views within that of the reference's; `under` holds it at most that above, `over` at least that below. Tolerances are about one standard deviation of the reference's own frames, rounded, tighter where a rule asks no more than the reference shows. `cargo xtask looks` shoots the views and prints the table.",
  "rules": {
    "light": "Lit and exposed as the reference",
    "grade": "Coloured as the reference",
    "shade": "Shade is soft and takes the sky's colour",
    "plants": "Plants are communities with height and self-shadow",
    "ground": "Ground layers blend by height and noise",
    "tint": "Nothing reads as a debug tint",
    "far": "Far things keep the near things' light",
    "horizon": "The horizon is never empty",
    "textured": "Every surface is textured in the style",
    "eye": "What the eye meets is the reference's",
    "leaves": "Leaves read as leaves"
  },
